ws","records":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","change":"El Centro's nights warmed over the long run. Its days have warmed since 1982.","rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 78\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>78\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 80\u00b0F, and the record is 92\u00b0F (1934). The low of <strong>60\u00b0F</strong> was the 3rd warmest November 13 low of 102 since 1925.","t_rec":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","p_rec":"If El Centro's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, El Centro has set <strong class=\"sig\">31 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 96 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">148 record highs</strong>, far more than the 96 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (59). El Centro's all-time high is 122\u00b0F, on June 20, 2017.","t_chg":"El Centro's nights warmed over the long run. Its days have warmed since 1982.","p_chg":"Across 92 complete years: El Centro's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.41\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.31 to +0.51), about +3.9\u00b0F since 1927. El Centro's average high shows no clear change: +0.08\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.18) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1982, lows show no clear change and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.47\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.19 to +0.76). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in all 12 months. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"El Centro's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.08 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 2.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 1983 (5.72 in); the driest, 2021 (0.02 in). El Centro almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 26 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}